      "JUDY: It’s okay, we’ll get you some dry clothes at the house.\nBECCA DARLING: I’m... gonna... die...",
      "JUDY: This wasn’t a chemical spill. They’re burning the bodies. It must be bacteriological, viral. Something that spreads by human contact. Or the…\nBECCA DARLING: The air? -- it was in the water.\nJUDY: It was. It must have more than one mode of transmission. Or mutated or something, who knows.",
      "JUDY: You all right?\nBECCA DARLING: I feel sick.\nJUDY: What kind of sick?\nBECCA DARLING: Dizzy.",
      "BECCA DARLING: I saw someone.\nJUDY: Let’s go.",
      "JUDY: Over there!!\nBECCA DARLING: I don’t wanna die like this!"
    ]
